 session 2:
 Features of java 8:
 1.lambda expression:
 similar to methods,
 but they do not need a name
 and they can be implemented right in the body of method
 -You can write it directly inside another method instead of creating a separate method.
-Reduces boilerplate code.
 example:
 (x,y)->x+y

 2.stream API
 -java stream API for bulk data Operation on collection
 -It allows developers to perform operations like filtering, sorting, and mapping data in a more readable and efficient way.
-Before Java 8, if we wanted to process a list (filter, sort, etc.), we had to write many loops and lines of code.

3.date and time Apl:
packeage: java.time
java 8 offers a new date - time API

4.base64 encode and decode

5.
method reference and constructor reference

6. funcrtional interface
-one abstract mehtod
-we don't need to use @functionlanterface
-Example:
 Runnable, Comparator

 7. Default Methods in Interfaces
   Interfaces can now have method implementation using default.

   Example:
   default void show() {
       System.out.println("Hello");
   }

8. Static Methods in Interfaces
 Interfaces can contain static methods.
 Example:
 static void display(){
     System.out.println("Static method");
 }

 9. Method References

 Short way to call methods using ::.

 Example:

 System.out::println

 10.Optional Class
    Used to avoid NullPointerException.
    Example:

    Optional<String> name = Optional.of("Java");

 11.Parallel Streams
    Allows parallel processing of data.
    Example:
    list.parallelStream().forEach(System.out::println);

 12. Nashorn JavaScript Engine
    Allows running JavaScript code inside Java.

 13. Collectors Class
    Used with Stream API to collect results
    Example:

    list.stream().collect(Collectors.toList());

 14. forEach() Method
    Iterates through collections easily.
    Example:
    list.forEach(System.out::println);
